// the index is an ordinary argument, judged by the ordinary conversion rule against the operand the
// contract declares - so a `string` where a `usize` belongs is a refusal and not a codegen throw
//
// the *wording* is B20's, not this case's: `array<T>` declares a writable and a read-only element
// contract, so the set holds two arity-2 candidates and neither is viable. with one candidate the
// short-circuit inside match_function would earn the sharper "cannot implicitly convert 'string' to
// 'usize'" instead, which is exactly the diagnostic B20 is about
array<int32> $a = [1];

echo $a["nope"];
